-- title:
--   Weighted host outside two specified cover classes
-- statement:
--   There exists one infinite positive-integer host H with a base-two finite-prime weighted witness and divergent reciprocal sum, with neither strengthened positive-cover data nor logarithmic-budget cover data. Every infinite subset of this same host has an irrational reciprocal Mersenne series at every integer base at least two. This is a later same-host separation, not paper Theorem 1 or the paper's A_star example.
--
--   **How to inspect this proof.** The `:= by sorry` in the formal statement above is Prove2Me's challenge placeholder. The accepted Solution is stored separately under **View graph → Solutions & Sketches**, which currently asks a signed-out reader to log in. The [pinned public Lean source](https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos-lean/blob/c93c2e4dd86a2e317e0cb650ea244fee1afd59c2/ErdosProblems/Erdos257/PaperCompleteR8/AnalyticSeparationReturn.lean#L14-L25) contains a proof body for this exact statement. The [#257 paper's related separation](https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/6917e15ec4abc2623512254da93221e446eeb707/paper/257/erdos-257-mersenne-support-subseries.tex#L569-L573) gives context but does not include this Lean theorem's additional log-budget clause. The assertion for every infinite support remains open.
